    private fun story3() = EnStory(
        storyId = "adv_old_man_and_sea",
        chapters = listOf(
            EnChapter(1, "The Old Fisherman", listOf(
                "He was an old man who fished alone in a skiff in the Gulf Stream and he had gone eighty-four days now without taking a fish, and in the first forty days a boy had been with him, but after forty days without a fish the boy's parents had told him that the old man was now definitely and finally salao.",
                "Salao is the worst form of unlucky, and the boy had gone at their orders in another boat which caught three good fish the first week, and it made the boy sad to see the old man come in each day with his skiff empty.",
                "The old man was thin and gaunt with deep wrinkles in the back of his neck, and the brown blotches of the benevolent skin cancer the sun brings from its reflection on the tropic sea were on his cheeks.",
                "Everything about him was old except his eyes, and they were the same color as the sea and were cheerful and undefeated.",
                "The boy loved the old man, and he had been with him in the boat since he was five years old, and he knew that the old man was not truly salao, that he was simply the victim of a long run of bad luck.",
                "But the boy's parents had insisted, and so the boy had gone to another boat, though every evening he would come to the old man's shack and help him carry his gear and talk about the day's fishing.",
                "The old man did not blame the boy, for he understood the position that the boy was in, and he was glad that the boy was catching fish, for he loved the boy as though he were his own son.",
                "But even so, there was a loneliness in the old man's life that could not be filled, a loneliness that came from fishing alone, from living alone, from being alone in a world that had no place for him anymore.",
                "His wife had died many years before, and he kept her picture on the wall, and sometimes he would look at it and feel a sadness that he could not fully express, a sadness that was older than his loneliness, older than his poverty, older than his age.",
                "He had been a great fisherman once, and he had fished with the best of them, and he had known the sea as few men have ever known it, and he had brought in fish that were the wonder of the harbor.",
                "But those days were gone, and now he was just an old man in a small boat, and the other fishermen pitied him or ignored him or laughed at him behind his back.",
                "But the old man did not care, for he had his pride, and he had his skill, and he had his love of the sea, and these things were enough for him, or at least they would have to be.",
                "The boy brought him food that evening, and they talked about baseball, about the great DiMaggio, about the heroes of the sport, and for a while the old man was happy.",
                "And then, as the night fell, the old man went to bed, and he dreamed of the lions on the beach in Africa, the lions that he had seen in his youth, the lions that came to him now in his sleep.",
                "In the morning, he would go out again, into the deep waters of the Gulf Stream, to try his luck once more, to prove to himself and to the world that he was still a fisherman.",
